WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.438 --> 00:00:04.222
Unit eighteen. Vaccines and Community Immunity!

2
00:00:05.134 --> 00:00:08.484
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:11.811
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:11.861 --> 00:00:15.991
Today we learn about Vaccines and Community Immunity. Let's go!

5
00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:20.583
Vaccine. Say it with me. Vaccine!

6
00:00:24.084 --> 00:00:27.384
Immunity. Say it with me. Immunity!

7
00:00:30.885 --> 00:00:34.602
Community. Say it with me. Community!

8
00:00:38.053 --> 00:00:41.686
Herd immunity. Say it with me. Herd immunity!

9
00:00:45.219 --> 00:00:48.803
Outbreak. Say it with me. Outbreak!

10
00:00:52.299 --> 00:00:55.765
Schedule. Say it with me. Schedule!

11
00:00:59.243 --> 00:01:02.793
Measles. Say it with me. Measles!

12
00:01:06.269 --> 00:01:09.618
Protect. Say it with me. Protect!

13
00:01:13.132 --> 00:01:23.966
Vaccines build immunity. When enough people are vaccinated, herd immunity protects the whole community, including babies. Following the schedule prevents an outbreak of diseases like measles.

14
00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.976
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:28.776 --> 00:01:33.890
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.090
Community!

17
00:01:36.026 --> 00:01:41.283
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:42.483
Measles!

19
00:01:43.404 --> 00:01:49.009
Did you know? Measles spreads so easily that most people need to be vaccinated to protect a community!

20
00:01:49.059 --> 00:01:50.973
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:59.450
Think and answer. Who is protected by herd immunity?

22
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.650
Great answer!

23
00:02:01.643 --> 00:02:06.129
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:06.179 --> 00:02:08.684
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

